/-!
# An ample scaling boundary with independent coefficients

Let `(X, B)` be a klt pair with an effective real boundary on a normal `ℚ`-factorial projective
variety of dimension at least two over an algebraically closed field of characteristic zero. There
is an effective real divisor `H = ∑ⱼ hⱼ Hⱼ` such that the `Hⱼ` are distinct ample Cartier prime
divisors not in the support of `B` whose numerical classes span `N¹(X)_ℝ`, the coefficients
`0 < hⱼ < 1` are linearly independent over the subfield `k₀ ⊆ ℝ` generated by the coefficients of
`B`, the pair `(X, B + H)` is klt and `K_X + B + H` is ample. This is the scaling divisor with
which the real minimal model program with scaling is run.

The proof follows the source. Finitely many Cartier divisors span `N¹(X)_ℝ`; twisting them by a
multiple of one ample divisor gives an ample basis `D₁, …, D_l`. By openness of the ample cone,
`K_X + B + (ν/4) ∑ⱼ Dⱼ` is ample for `ν ≫ 0`, and `𝒪_X(νDⱼ)` is very ample. The `hⱼ ∈ (1/4, 1/2)`
are chosen one at a time outside the span of their predecessors over the countable coefficient
field. The `Hⱼ` are general members of `|νDⱼ|`, chosen one at a time: a general member of a very
ample system is integral (Bertini's irreducibility theorem), and on a log resolution of the pair
built so far its pull-back is reduced and crosses the snc boundary normally (Bertini), so the
crepant boundary of the new pair is snc with coefficients less than one. Finally
`K_X + B + ∑ hⱼ Hⱼ = (K_X + B + (ν/4) ∑ Dⱼ) + ∑ (hⱼ - 1/4) Hⱼ + (1/4) ∑ div(uⱼ)` with
`Hⱼ = νDⱼ + div(uⱼ)` ample, and adding real multiples of principal divisors keeps ampleness.

## Main results

* `MMP.Fourfold.IsRealKltPair.exists_isRelativelyAmple_add_linearIndependent`.

## Implementation notes

Each `Hⱼ` is recorded twice: as a prime divisor `Pⱼ` and as a Cartier divisor `Eⱼ` whose Weil
divisor is `Pⱼ` (`MMP.Intersection.IsWeilDivisorOfCartier`); the class of `Eⱼ` is the element of
`N¹(X)_ℝ = MMP.Fourfold.NumericalDivisorClasses`. Ampleness of `K_X + B + H` is ampleness over
`Spec k` of the `ℝ`-divisor, `MMP.Flips.IsRelativelyAmple`, and is asserted for every canonical
divisor `K_X`.

Klt is tested on one smooth model by
`MMP.Fourfold.AmpleFloorLowering.logDiscrepancy_pos_of_isSmoothResolution`. The Bertini theorem on
a resolution and the zero schemes of sections of divisorial sheaves are the arguments of
`MMP.Fourfold.IsRealDltPair.exists_isRealKltPair_sub_add_of_isAmple`, repeated here for a klt
pair and a very ample system. The Cartier divisor `Eⱼ` with Weil divisor `Hⱼ` is glued from the
local generators of the ideal of the zero scheme of the section cutting out `Hⱼ`; its class in
`N¹(X)_ℝ` is `ν [Gⱼ]`, where `Gⱼ` is the Cartier divisor of `Dⱼ`, as both have the same degree on
every proper curve.

## References

* [J. Kollár, S. Mori, *Birational geometry of algebraic varieties*][KollarMori]
-/

